# No Python in scripts

**Decided repeatedly (e.g. 2026-10-14):** packaging, gates, scaffolding, and
dev tooling under `scripts/` and `apps/*/scripts/` are **bash** (or Rust
`tools/` crates) — **not** Python.

## Do

- Write new tooling as `.sh` (preferred) or a small Rust binary under `tools/`.
- Prefer `gawk` / `jq` / `curl` / existing bash helpers over spinning up `python3`.
- When replacing a retired `.py`, delete it and update `docs/DEV.md` + any
  Cursor rule that still shows `python3 …`.

## Do not

```text
❌ Add or revive scripts/*.py or apps/*/scripts/*.py for product tooling
❌ Wire load_kumkaj_env / packaging gates to python3
❌ Document python3 as the “official” way to scaffold or check UI translations
❌ “Just this once” Python for a bulk fill — use bash, agents editing TSVs, or a Rust tool
```

```text
✅ ./scripts/check-ui-translations.sh
✅ ./scripts/scaffold-ui-translations.sh
✅ cargo test -p <crate> --lib every_catalogue_language_translates_every_key
```

Exception: throwaway probes under `local/` (gitignored) may use anything;
they must not become the documented or gated path.
